<p>The Africa Centres for Disease Control and Prevention confirmed Friday an Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of the Congo’s eastern Ituri province, with 246 suspected cases and 65 deaths, mainly in the Mongwalu and Rwampara health zones. Preliminary laboratory results detected Ebola virus in 13 of 20 samples, with four deaths among laboratory-confirmed cases and additional suspected cases reported in Bunia, Ituri’s provincial capital. Africa CDC said initial findings suggested a strain other than Zaire and that sequencing was underway. Uganda separately confirmed a Bundibugyo Ebola infection in a Congolese man treated in Kampala, while health agencies moved to reinforce surveillance around Ituri’s borders with Uganda and South Sudan.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/17WJQjbHY_YhIDhiEksMA2la9WhYuarblCHNSRW-YEwmu2yh2RxkPOrgd9M2dyavPjZDbP8K4rVOcYzhPppqxgBMzSozCkxSbL5QkKq1gznWgAhmdLjxjz3WWVsuxVSRQTm1CEZKBnPEVgOxenpLKBaFYLVG7NozMhKPTRacWMrK6s7TJ7LueyDyM4coOCOVdTqbdjaTM_NTRA0yPTK8OBOQsOrdZ2zWDezLlDppE9nXBy20L-lXCsy7Bi_prjQ5pNI1ZThwFjfmTU71WA' alt='Thermometers at the entrance of an Ebola treatment centre in Butembo, Democratic Republic of Congo, in 2019.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Spread risks: Africa CDC cited urban conditions in Bunia and Rwampara, mining-related mobility in Mongwalu and heavy movement near the Uganda and South Sudan borders as risks for further spread.</li><li>Logistics: Ituri is a remote eastern province with poor road networks and areas more than 1,000 kilometers from Kinshasa, conditions that can slow supplies and response teams.</li><li>Security context: Armed group attacks in parts of Ituri have killed dozens and displaced thousands over the past year, adding insecurity to the public health response.</li><li>Case finding: Health officials reported gaps in contact tracing and said local authorities were trying to identify people who may have been exposed to the virus.</li></ul><blockquote>This is an imported case from DRC. The country has not yet confirmed a local case - Uganda Ministry of Health</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Gabriel Nsakala: The public health professor said Congo and local health workers have experience and infrastructure from earlier Ebola responses, but expertise and equipment must be moved quickly into place. (<a href='https://www.bastillepost.com/hongkong/article/16017345-%e5%89%9b%e6%9e%9c%e4%bc%8a%e6%b3%a2%e6%8b%89%e7%96%ab%e6%83%85%e5%a5%aa65%e5%91%bd-%e9%9d%9e%e6%b4%b2%e7%96%be%e6%8e%a7%e4%b8%ad%e5%bf%83%e9%97%9c%e6%b3%a8%e8%94%93%e5%bb%b6%e9%a2%a8%e9%9a%aa'>Bastille Post</a>)</li><li>Uganda Ministry of Health: The ministry said Uganda tested a sample taken from the patient after DRC reported its outbreak, confirming the Bundibugyo strain. (<a href='https://www.channelstv.com/2026/05/15/uganda-health-ministry-confirms-ebola-outbreak-one-dead/'>Channels Television</a>)</li><li>Jean-Jacques Muyembe: The Congolese virologist, who heads the National Institute for Biomedical Research in Kinshasa, said all but one of Congo’s previous Ebola outbreaks had involved the Zaire strain, while authorities had not completed final identification of the current strain. (<a href='https://www.infomoney.com.br/mundo/agencia-africana-de-saude-anuncia-surto-de-ebola-no-congo-com-65-mortes-suspeitas/'>InfoMoney</a>)</li><li>World Health Organization: Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus said WHO allocated $500,000 from its emergency fund to support surveillance, contact tracing and other response work. (<a href='https://www.annahar.com/international/world/310323/مراكز-مكافحة-الأمراض-الأفريقية-تعلن-تفشي-إيبولا-في-الكونغو-مع-65-وفاة'>Annahar</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/health/confirmed-ebola-outbreak-in-congo-says-african-public-health-agency/article70981943.ece'>African public health agency announces new Ebola outbreak in Congo, 65 suspected deaths</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cze2wpk7y